        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Draining a water heater is simple if you follow the order: heat off, cold supply closed, water cooled, hot faucet open, drain, flush, refill completely, then heat back on. The two steps that cause the most damage when skipped are turning the heat off first and waiting until the tank is full to turn it back on.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Done once a year, it keeps sediment from building up, protects the bottom of the tank and the lower element, and gives you a regular look at the heater's condition. If what comes out tells you the tank is near the end, our gas water heater picks are the next stop.
          </p>
